 ],
 "literal": "Unlike the spears of others, in this village / the warrior's spear indeed possesses great dignity! / Smeared and mingled with dust on its dark iron back, / even if it lies in the thatched roof of the hut, it will lie. / Adorned with garlands by auspicious women, / while the sweet-voiced irumpai lute resounds, / roaming through the clear-water ponds and the streets, / even if it goes making the entire earth tremble, it will go. There, / of kings with vast ocean-like armies, / its march into the faces of the great war-elephants never ceases!",
 "translation": "Unlike the spears of others, the spear of the warrior of this village possesses great dignity! Sometimes, with soot and dust smeared on its dark iron back, it lies tucked away in the thatched roof of his humble hut. At other times, adorned with garlands by auspicious women while the sweet-voiced irumpai lute resounds, it roams through the clear-water ponds and streets, making the entire earth tremble. And when war comes, its relentless charge straight into the faces of the great war-elephants of kings with ocean-like armies never ceases!",
 "modern": "பிறருடைய வேலைப் போல அல்லாமல், இந்த ஊர் வீரனுடைய வேல் பெரும் பெருமையைக் கொண்டிருக்கிறது. அதன் இரும்புப் புறத்தில் தூசு படிந்து, அது ஒரு குடிலின் கூரைக்குள்ளே சும்மா கிடந்தாலும் கிடக்கும். மங்கல மகளிர் அதற்கு மாலை சூட்டி, இனிய ஓசையுடைய இரும்பை யாழின் இசை ஒலிக்க, தெளிந்த நீருடைய குளங்களிலும் தெருக்களிலும் வலம் வந்து, பூமி முழுதும் அதிரும்படி அது சென்றாலும் செல்லும். அங்கே, கடல் போன்ற பெரும் படையைக் கொண்ட அரசர்களின் பெரிய போர் யானைகளின் முகத்தில் பாய்ந்து செல்லும் அதன் வேகம் ஒருபோதும் குறையாது!",
 "explanation": "This poem belongs to the Puram genre, specifically the Vākai tiṇai and the Mūtiṉ Mullai theme, which celebrates the ancestral valor of a warrior family. The poet Viriyūr Kiḻār praises the unique and dignified nature of the spear belonging to a local warrior. In times of peace, the spear lies neglected and covered in soot, tucked into the thatched roof of a humble hut. In times of celebration, it is adorned with garlands by auspicious women and paraded through the streets to the sweet music of lutes, making the earth tremble. When war erupts, it fearlessly and relentlessly charges straight into the faces of the massive war-elephants of powerful kings. This contrast between the spear's humble domestic resting place and its fierce battlefield glory highlights the innate, unpretentious bravery of the warrior.",
 "model": "gemini-3.5-flash",
 "generated": "2026-11-26"
}